docs/modules/ROOT/pages/access-control.adoc:96:In essence, we will be defining multiple _roles_, each allowed to perform different sets of actions. An account may have, for example, 'moderator', 'minter' or 'admin' roles, which you will then check for instead of simply using `only_owner`. This check can be enforced through the `only_role` modifier. Separately, you will be able to define rules for how accounts can be granted a role, have it revoked, and more.
